@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`

-- hvac-tests-calendars.l4 -- the calendars of days of rest, recess or holiday that the tests
-- supply, as the input Interpretation Law s 10(c) needs.
--
-- These are ILLUSTRATIONS chosen by the tests, not a statement of any Israeli calendar: no holiday
-- is in them, and which days are days of rest "על פי חיקוק" (under an enactment) for a given
-- period is not something this encoding can know.  Saturday only and Friday plus Saturday are the
-- two the date correction asked for; Sundays is a third, used only to show that a function which
-- never moves with the first two does move with another calendar.
-- 4 January 2020 was a Saturday, so a day is a Saturday when its day count is a multiple of seven
-- from that one.  The calendars are right for days from 4 January 2020 on.

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Saturdays are days of rest` day MEANS
    ((Day day MINUS Day (YMD 2020 1 4)) MODULO 7) EQUALS 0

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest` day MEANS
       ((Day day MINUS Day (YMD 2020 1 4)) MODULO 7) EQUALS 0
    OR ((Day day MINUS Day (YMD 2020 1 4)) MODULO 7) EQUALS 6

GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sundays are days of rest` day MEANS
    ((Day day MINUS Day (YMD 2020 1 4)) MODULO 7) EQUALS 1

-- Positive controls: the weekdays of days the tests lean on, checked on a calendar (Python's
-- datetime) when the tests were designed, and here against the L4.
-- Saturday 2026-04-04 and Friday 2026-04-03; Sunday 2026-04-05.
#ASSERT `Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2026 4 4)
#ASSERT NOT `Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2026 4 3)
#ASSERT NOT `Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2026 4 5)
#ASSERT `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2026 4 3)
#ASSERT `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2026 4 4)
#ASSERT NOT `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2026 4 5)
-- Saturday 2027-01-16 (18 months from 16 July 2025); Friday 2027-04-16; Sunday 2028-07-16.
#ASSERT `Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2027 1 16)
#ASSERT `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2027 4 16)
#ASSERT `Sundays are days of rest` (YMD 2028 7 16)
#ASSERT NOT `Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2025 7 16)
#ASSERT NOT `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2025 7 16)
-- Saturday 2029-06-30, Friday 2028-06-30; Saturday 2030-01-12.
#ASSERT `Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2029 6 30)
#ASSERT `Fridays and Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2028 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2028 6 30)
#ASSERT `Saturdays are days of rest` (YMD 2030 1 12)
